{
 "version": "3.1.0",
 "note": "Runtime lookup table only. Keep rationale short here; branch on these rules instead of re-deriving them in app code.",
 "contract": "Resolve `series` first and build the per-hour series. SUM=add member areas. WEIGHTED_MEAN=sum(x*w)/sum(w) per hour, null when sum(w)==0 (then try fallbackWeight). MEAN=unweighted mean of areas. Charts and stats run on that series only; never sort or box-plot a summed INTENSIVE column. `temporal`=SUM means a period total is meaningful; MEAN means it is not (MW summed over hours is MWh). `derived`={minuend,subtrahend,op} marks a CALCULATED column: it has no source column, its plane is filled at ingest per area from the two operands, and it is present only when both are. op=`sub` (default) is valid ONLY for same-unit EXTENSIVE operands, where sum(a-b) == sum(a)-sum(b). op=`div` does NOT commute with the area collapse, so such a column MUST also be series=WEIGHTED_MEAN weighted by its DENOMINATOR (subtrahend): sum((a/b)*b)/sum(b) == sum(a)/sum(b) restores the ratio of sums. Any other series or weight on a div column is a plausible wrong number.",
